[{"id":"VRCE-2-102-1","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":102,"verse":1,"english":"Knowing that Rāma was wroth, Vasiştha said, Jābāli knows the departure of the creature to the next world and their return thence.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.621,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-110-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2102001","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"285b6f53e49c673ca8958d81eefe58818df9ceaeb9a586ee8167028a039c03ee","compact":"b25dd03bd7099079f2b06848214a7531da92939650d8bac4f4cfc8c1ec53ac89","nasal":"b25dd03bd7099079f2b06848214a7531da92939650d8bac4f4cfc8c1ec53ac89"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-102-2","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":102,"verse":2,"english":"Anxious of making the turn back, he had spoken thus. Do you now, O lord of the world, learn the genesis of creatures from me. Water was everywhere. The earth was constructed therein. Then sprang the self-create Brahmā along with all the celestials.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.484,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-110-2","DUTT-2-110-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2102002","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5875989f362e32237f3cc3ac61b3121d52f544128503f8c07c600097f0c119a4","compact":"7623f721c47eb5cdf3e53c766cde46e3e8653a10127f60edf7043d47429e3427","nasal":"c74dad38732df25583f34d22f4e0ef9498f02422f4dec219d23be2eeb62bb4ce"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-102-3","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":102,"verse":3,"english":"Having become a boar, he raised up the earth, and along with his sons of subdued souls created everything.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.873,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-110-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2102003","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"