u by Manu. Do you know Ikşvāku as the first kind in Ayodhyā.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-110-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2102006","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e7595a3a2b40c6aa6fe0d764abd1b3cda8cb837b13fd8fa7ce603df68ddcc48e","compact":"99af2b650557cb66e7ce3110df56d677b604275a7b8ebf28c6ce20a99cf92c45","nasal":"99af2b650557cb66e7ce3110df56d677b604275a7b8ebf28c6ce20a99cf92c45"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-102-7","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":102,"verse":7,"english":"The graceful Kukşi is known as the son of Iksvāku. And, O hero, Kuksi's son was Vikuksi.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.722,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-110-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2102007","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"dfe4f0a60ec9bd0182ec76e7eda119b9deaf6809e085b5fc49c33b1e7bef99f4","compact":"2973fc038a043a3790dc68d26a50c5f9b48a8c9d66c41b410639298b89fe94aa","nasal":"2973fc038a043a3790dc68d26a50c5f9b48a8c9d66c41b410639298b89fe94aa"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-102-8","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":102,"verse":8,"english":"Vikukși had the powerful Bāņa possessed of exceeding energy for his son. Bāna had the mighty-armed Anaranya of high austerities for his son.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.787,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-110-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2102008","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"82553410fb7beb87fc4a6fc79f3696bb24d7b33f03ebd47d9671cecf08bc0485","compact":"95a566749c4569bef70698edfa7ab64519525613d43daa881fd59a1931775be2","nasal":"95a566749c4569bef70698edfa7ab64519525613d43daa881fd59a1931775be2"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-102-9","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":102,"verse":9,"e