1","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":102,"verse":21,"english":"Asamanja's son was the puissant Ansumat. Dilipa is the son of Ansumat and Dilipa's son is Bhagiratha.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.852,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-110-21"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2102021","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"791688989ed79858993a0a28d923f9d353310648324a681a6a729808357fac18","compact":"5f6a92e4da026b9b18c4899705a6c30a5345b5f56e20f4cf15715a852b98cbe9","nasal":"baff3ff366d61b177b49b8df45f4c293dc7944c9349575b0e1f0be047a8a68ac"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-102-22","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":102,"verse":22,"english":"From Bhagiratha sprang Kakutstha; from whom the Kākutsthas came to be well known. Kakutstha had Raghu for his son; after whom have been named the Rāghavas.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.836,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-110-22"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2102022","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"603d1f3c93a7e7a93a5f56cf5dd876727fc857ce753c8b2b97b0d4646d998796","compact":"a5d39109338ef36e9817468df04d6818c0274f6a943e0163faf16fe6b190bcbc","nasal":"a5d39109338ef36e9817468df04d6818c0274f6a943e0163faf16fe6b190bcbc"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-102-23","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":102,"verse":23,"english":"Raghu's son is the energetic Pravědha, who are human beings. He is known on earth under such names as Kalmāşapāda, Saudāsa.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-110-23"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2102023","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"51324ad19435b9dc72174f9a60e40f52ba412b1240a27112912c6bc19d41c696","compact":"92fa3aefb1ca2741c39e2edfe18c8c2504c7e35d448678877eceecc8c